ction_and_inverse_function_105b6f88_008","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"If $f\\colon X\\to Y$ is bijective and $f(x) = y$, what is $f^{-1}(y)$?","options":["$y$","$x$","$f(y)$","$0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"6a3904a27d1b0d8b33d3580d"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_bijection_and_inverse_function_105b6f88_009","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which missing condition prevents a function from having an inverse without ambiguity?","options":["Being written with the letter $f$","Having a real-valued codomain","Injectivity","Being a polynomial"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"830078e7268070fd20672d0f"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_bijection_and_inverse_function_105b6f88_010","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which missing condition prevents every element of the codomain from being assigned an inverse value?","options":["Associativity","Boundedness","Differentiability","Surjectivity"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"e7242a404a3d7fccbade9cd1"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_bijection_and_inverse_function_105b6f88_011","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"If $f\\colon X\\to Y$ is injective but not surjective, what goes wrong with defining $f^{-1}$ on all of $Y$?","options":["Some $y\\in Y$ has too many preimages","Every $y\\in Y$ has exactly one preimage","Some $y\\in Y$ has no preimage","The domain $X$ is automatically empty"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"51bf9e8b58512b1ec9301545"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_bijection_and_inverse_function_105b6f88_012","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"If $f\\colon X\\to Y$ is surjective but not injective, what goes wrong with defining $f^{-1}$?","options":["No output has any preimage","The inverse must equal the identity on $X$","Some output may have several preimages","The function becomes bounded"],"answe